---
import DocLayout from "../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
const headings = [
  { label: "Run from the flake", href: "#run" },
  { label: "NixOS module", href: "#nixos" },
  { label: "Service policy", href: "#service-policy" },
  { label: "Secrets", href: "#secrets" },
  { label: "Home Manager", href: "#home-manager" },
  { label: "Flake outputs", href: "#outputs" },
];
---

<DocLayout
  title="Nix installation"
  description="Run Scorch directly from its flake or enable the client and service declaratively with the exported NixOS and Home Manager modules."
  eyebrow="Deployment"
  headings={headings}
  previous={{ label: "Agent Skill", href: "/skill/" }}
>
  <h2 id="run">Run from the flake</h2>
  <p>
    The release flake exposes separate packages and apps for the HTTP-only
    client and the runtime-owning service. Pin a release tag for reproducible
    deployments. Nix downloads the matching GitHub Actions release archive and
    patches it for the Nix store; it does not compile Scorch locally.
  </p>
  <pre><code>nix run github:Fractal-Tess/scorch/v0.3.0#scorch -- --help
nix run github:Fractal-Tess/scorch/v0.3.0#scorchd -- --help</code></pre>
  <p>Install either package into a profile:</p>
  <pre><code>nix profile install github:Fractal-Tess/scorch/v0.3.0#scorch
nix profile install github:Fractal-Tess/scorch/v0.3.0#scorchd</code></pre>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Linux support.</strong> The embedded Obscura V8 renderer is packaged for
    <code>x86_64-linux</code> and <code>aarch64-linux</code>. No external
    browser package or executable is required.
  </div>

  <h2 id="nixos">Enable both on NixOS</h2>
  <p>
    Add Scorch as an input, import its module, install <code>scorch</code>, and
    start
    <code>scorchd</code>. The default service binds only to loopback.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Default endpoint.</strong> The service listens on
    <code>http://127.0.0.1:33000</code>, and the client uses the same URL by
    default. Set <code>programs.scorch.apiUrl</code> when you want NixOS to export
    an explicit <code>SCORCH_API_URL</code> for login sessions.
  </div>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  inputs = &#123;
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
    scorch.url = "github:Fractal-Tess/scorch/v0.3.0";
  &#125;;

  outputs = &#123; nixpkgs, scorch, ... &#125;: &#123;
    nixosConfigurations.host = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem &#123;
      system = "x86_64-linux";
      modules = [
        scorch.nixosModules.default
        (&#123; ... &#125;: &#123;
          programs.scorch.enable = true;

          services.scorchd = &#123;
            enable = true;
            address = "127.0.0.1";
            port = 33000;
          &#125;;
        &#125;)
      ];
    &#125;;
  &#125;;
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>Apply the host configuration and inspect the service:</p>
  <pre><code>sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#host
systemctl status scorchd
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:33000/ready | jq
scorch search "rust web extraction" --limit 3</code></pre>

  <h2 id="service-policy">Configure service policy</h2>
  <pre><code>services.scorchd = &#123;
  enable = true;
  obscuraStealth = true;
  maxConcurrency = 4;
  maxResponseBytes = 5 * 1024 * 1024;
  jobTtlSeconds = 900;
  searchEngines = [
    "bing"
    "duckduckgo"
    "naver"
    "wikipedia"
  ];
  logLevel = "scorch=info";
  logFormat = "json";
&#125;;</code></pre>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Default</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td><code>programs.scorch.enable</code></td><td
            ><code>false</code></td
          ><td>Install the HTTP client and MCP adapter.</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>programs.scorch.apiUrl</code></td><td><code>null</code></td
          ><td>Export <code>SCORCH_API_URL</code> to login sessions.</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>services.scorchd.enable</code></td><td
            ><code>false</code></td
          ><td>Start the hardened systemd service.</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>address</code> / <code>port</code></td><td
            ><code>127.0.0.1:33000</code></td
          ><td>Configure the API listener.</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>openFirewall</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td
            >Open the configured TCP port.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>searchEngines</code></td><td
            ><code>bing, duckduckgo, naver, wikipedia</code></td
          ><td>Set the server allowlist available to search requests.</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>environmentFile</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td
            >Load credentials without putting them in the Nix store.</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    The module asserts that the search-engine allowlist is non-empty. Requests
    that omit an engine subset use allowed Bing and DuckDuckGo adapters. Obscura
    is embedded, so the service does not need a browser package, executable
    path, or browser-selection policy. Authentication and TLS remain the
    responsibility of an external gateway.
  </p>

  <h2 id="secrets">Load search credentials safely</h2>
  <p>
    Do not place API keys directly in a Nix expression: evaluated values can
    enter the world-readable Nix store. Point the module at a runtime secret
    managed by sops-nix, agenix, or another provisioner that can write a runtime <code
      >KEY=value</code
    > file.
  </p>
  <pre><code>services.scorchd = &#123;
  enable = true;
  searchEngines = [ "bing" "brave" "wikipedia" ];
  environmentFile = "/run/secrets/scorchd.env";
&#125;;</code></pre>
  <pre><code># /run/secrets/scorchd.env
SCORCH_BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=replace-at-deploy-time</code></pre>
  <p>
    Google requires both <code>SCORCH_GOOGLE_SEARCH_API_KEY</code> and <code
      >SCORCH_GOOGLE_SEARCH_ENGINE_ID</code
    >. The module's general <code>environment</code> option is intended only for non-secret
    overrides.
  </p>

  <h2 id="home-manager">Home Manager</h2>
  <p>
    Use the Home Manager module when only the user-level client is needed. It
    does not manage <code>scorchd</code>; run the service through NixOS or
    another process supervisor.
  </p>
  <p>Inside your flake's <code>outputs</code> function:</p>
  <pre><code>homeConfigurations.user = home-manager.lib.homeManagerConfiguration &#123;
  pkgs = nixpkgs.legacyPackages.x86_64-linux;
  modules = [
    scorch.homeManagerModules.default
    &#123;
      home.username = "user";
      home.homeDirectory = "/home/user";
      home.stateVersion = "26.05";
      programs.scorch.enable = true;
    &#125;
  ];
&#125;;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="outputs">Flake outputs</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Output</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td><code>packages.&lt;system&gt;.scorch</code></td><td
            >HTTP-only CLI and MCP executable.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>packages.&lt;system&gt;.scorchd</code></td><td
            >API service with the embedded Obscura renderer.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>packages.&lt;system&gt;.skill</code></td><td
            >Installable Scorch Agent Skill.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>apps.&lt;system&gt;.scorch</code></td><td
            ><code>nix run</code> client app.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>apps.&lt;system&gt;.scorchd</code></td><td
            ><code>nix run</code> service app.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>nixosModules.default</code></td><td
            >NixOS client and systemd service configuration.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>homeManagerModules.default</code></td><td
            >User-level client configuration.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>overlays.default</code></td><td
            >All Scorch packages for direct package-set use.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>devShells.&lt;system&gt;.default</code></td><td
            >Rust, Bun, and development tools.</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <pre><code>nix flake show github:Fractal-Tess/scorch/v0.3.0</code></pre>
</DocLayout>
